# guard install output — per-clone local git-hooks dir wired via core.hooksPath
# (`hmd guard install`). Install output, not source. Lives in the working tree
# (not .git/) on purpose so a relative core.hooksPath survives a repo move.
# Also holds the SI-2 attestation runtime store (.heimdall/attestations/<id>.json):
# one record per commit/task, emitted by `heimdall-attest` and read by F2–F6 —
# per-checkout runtime state, never committed.
# Ignore the runtime home's CONTENTS (so the real config + secrets + the
# attestation store never commit) — but as `.heimdall/*` (not `.heimdall/`) so
# git still DESCENDS into the dir and the single un-ignore below can take effect.
.heimdall/*
.heimdall/attestations/
# The telemetry NDJSON event store (.heimdall/telemetry/events*.ndjson): per-
# checkout runtime metrics, local-first, NEVER committed. Already covered by
# `.heimdall/*` above; named explicitly so a future un-ignore exception can never
# accidentally leak it. The store stays gitleaks-CLEAN-by-construction (the scrubber
# keeps secrets out) — it is NEVER added to .gitleaks.toml's allowlist.
.heimdall/telemetry/
# EXCEPTION: the issue-loop config EXAMPLE is committed source (structure +
# env-var NAMES only, never secrets). The REAL config (.heimdall/issue-loop.config.json)
# and secrets file stay ignored by `.heimdall/*`; only this single .example is
# un-ignored so it can be committed.
!.heimdall/issue-loop.config.json.example

# designmatch v2 runtime ledger + quarantine (the regen-log.json hash-log and the
# tmp holding area are per-checkout runtime state, not source — never commit them).
.designmatch/

# superx runtime artifacts
.setup-done
.last-update-from
.superx-no-autocommit
.planning/dispatch/
.planning/metrics.jsonl
.planning/routing-overrides.json

# logs
*.log
/tmp/superx-*

# Playwright/npm artifacts from local smoke tests of designmatch scripts
skills/designmatch/scripts/node_modules/
skills/designmatch/scripts/package.json
skills/designmatch/scripts/package-lock.json

# Oracle-gate runtime artifacts: report.json is run.sh's typed OUTPUT, not source
evals/oracles/*/report.json
.planning/
# TEAM MODE P1 — the activity store is git-backed shared state (TM-1: git IS the
# coordination substrate). `.planning/` is broadly ignored above, so git won't
# descend to un-ignore a child unless each path segment is re-included first; we
# re-include the chain down to the activity dir, then un-ignore its records.
# Each instance's per-HAID activity record (.planning/ledger/activity/{slug}.json)
# is then tracked + synced across checkouts the same way claims/ is — one writer
# per file → conflict-free merges. The secret-scan gate (gitleaks) still scans
# these paths; the records are scrubbed secret-free by construction (heimdall-
# activity rejects any secret-shaped field before writing).
!.planning/
.planning/*
!.planning/ledger/
.planning/ledger/*
!.planning/ledger/activity/
# TEAM MODE P3 collision store (.planning/ledger/collisions/{branch-slug}.json):
# one record per current-branch scan of same-target-CHANGED collisions vs
# siblings. Tracked + synced across checkouts the same way claims/ and activity/
# are — one writer per file (keyed by the current branch's slug) → conflict-free
# merges. Records carry ONLY branch names + target (file/symbol) names + a
# classification (safe-textual vs flag-human); NEVER code, diffs, or secrets, so
# the gitleaks gate over these paths finds nothing (heimdall-collision writes the
# surface verdict, not the source).
!.planning/ledger/collisions/
# TEAM MODE P2 — the gate-verdict store is git-backed shared state, same as the
# activity store above. P2 (bin/heimdall-gate-surface) republishes SI-2's recorded
# verdict (gate names + pass/fail/blocked + a receipt loc) — secret-free by
# construction — into one per-HAID file (.planning/ledger/verdicts/{slug}.json) so
# a sibling checkout reads "what is PROVEN/BLOCKED where". The chain down to
# ledger/ is already re-included above; un-ignore the verdicts dir + its records.
# gitleaks still scans these paths; the summary carries no code/secret (the
# publisher scrubs every field through the telemetry _scrub discipline).
!.planning/ledger/verdicts/
.claude/
evals/benchmark/results.jsonl

# Git worktrees (heimdall isolation)
.worktrees/
